WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.922
Welcome to Module 14, the final module of IAN 601.

00:00:03.922 --> 00:00:13.037
This module is intentionally designed as a bridge into the machine learning course you will take next semester.

00:00:13.037 --> 00:00:16.802
We are not going to begin with a complicated algorithm.

00:00:16.802 --> 00:00:21.942
We will begin with something familiar: a simple algebraic formula.

00:00:21.942 --> 00:00:28.971
From there, we will ask what happens when the formula is unknown and we only have examples.

00:00:29.421 --> 00:00:32.493
That idea leads naturally into machine learning.

00:00:32.493 --> 00:00:41.593
We will move from a known line, to learning the line from data, to noisy observations, residuals, multiple features,

00:00:41.593 --> 00:00:47.478
numeric vectors, regression, classification, train and test data, evaluation metrics, and prediction.

00:00:47.478 --> 00:00:56.113
The purpose is to make machine learning feel like a continuation of what you already know rather than a completely

00:00:56.113 --> 00:00:59.063
separate subject.

00:00:59.063 --> 00:01:06.863
By the end, you should understand the structure of an ML workflow even if you have not yet studied every algorithm.
